Package: altarr
Title: Lazy Chunked Arrays as ALTREP Vectors
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Lazy chunked arrays for R, as ALTREP vectors with a 'dim'
    attribute and no class. Chunks come from a user-supplied fetch function,
    so any store (object storage, 'Zarr', 'GDAL') can sit behind them. Base
    R indexing, x[i] and x[cbind(i, j, k)], and reductions such as sum() and
    mean() become planned, batched reads of only the chunks they need, with
    a bounded chunk cache. altarr_extract() gives the same for rectangular
    regions, which base R's x[i, j, k] does not yet offer to ALTREP
    classes.
